// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2649319107" "You are in a serious situation, my young apprentice. It would appear that you are the greatest obstacle to all my lord's plans. I am bound to Arachnos, but still I am appalled that my Lord Recluse would continue on his course, even knowing that he risked the future of Arachnos and the world. But what could I do? I cannot disobey my Lord. And I could not even counsel you to challenge him, for to do so would only bring about the ruin you saw earlier. No, your only option is to flee. Well, flee or find some way to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>prove to Lord Recluse how great a threat you are without actually fighting him in the present time, where it could cause the end of the world.</A> But that would be nearly impossible to imagine. Even where you to find Lord Recluse at the point in the future he seeks where he was the one who defeats Statesman and were to attack him then, well, it would be difficult at best. But, bound to Arachnos as I am, I can only tell you how to escape to <i>any</i> point in time."
// AcceptString :
"P1885668442" "Take the hint and get Ghost Widow's help to 'Flee'"
// SendOffString :
"P813727507" "I confess I have grown fond of you, {VillainName}. Though we have clashed in past, you have done much for Arachnos, and therefore, much for me. So I can do you one last favor. Speak with Technician Grant Naylor on Nerva Archipelago. He should be able to re-align the Destiny Portal for you to reach any point in time within, oh, say, the next 10 to 15 years. I suppose he could even alter the portal so that you could come back, perhaps with a trophy of some sort."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P341828046" "Speak to Technician Naylor"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P123210417" "You should be asking Technician Naylor to help you hide from my Lord Recluse."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3163744992" "Oi, {VillainName}. I 'ear you're in big trouble. You want me to... WHA? You're kiddin' me, right? You want to go ta the moment of Lord Recluse's victory? Sure, I can do tha' for yeh. We've had people there a 'undred times before though, an' really you should be talkin' ta Operative Grillo, but you're the 'Destined One', I guess. Let me adjust this Harmonic Redistribuor for yah. Take it with ya next time ya go through tha Destiny Portal, an' that should fix things for yah."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2162470304" "So, it has come to this. I will do you this one last favor, and allow you to slip into the Destiny portal, {VillainName}. Perhaps, lost in the multiverse, you may be able to find your true destiny."
// RandomFameString :
"P1494239339" "{VillainName} sure is wearing a scary expression these days."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P725298946" "With that device from Technician Naylor, you should be able to reach exactly where you need to go. Still, I must counsel that you flee. Unless, of course, you think yourself able to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>defeat Lord Recluse at his moment of triumph then return and show him the proof</A>. That would be pure madness, even with a group of helpful cronies with you. No, that's a task that might even stop you."
// AcceptString :
"P2062524237" "Enter Destiny Portal and defeat Lord Recluse"
// SendOffString :
"P255431175" "Some times My Lord Recluse forgets that my spirit is bound to Arachnos, not necessarily to its leader. I hope you find just the time and place that you're looking for, {VillainName}."

